#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# acos

#% text
# `acos(x)` gives the principal inverse cosine of `x`, in `[0, pi]` for `-1 <= x <= 1`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact values at 0, `1/2`, `1/sqrt(2)`, `sqrt(3)/2`, 1 and their negatives; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Outside `[-1, 1]` the value is complex. Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values. `acos` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
acos(1/2)
#% output
#= (1/3)*pi

#% cell
acos(-1)
#% output
#= pi

#% cell
acos(0.3)
#% output
#= 1.2661036727794992

#% cell
acos(0)
#% output
#= (1/2)*pi

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Outside `[-1, 1]`:

#% cell
acos(2.0)
#% output
#= 0.0 + 1.3169578969248166im

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The angle between two vectors:

#% cell
u = [1, 2, 2]; v = [2, 1, -2]; acos(dot(u, v)/(norm(u)*norm(v)))
#% output
#= (1/2)*pi

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(acos(x), x)
#% output
#= -1/(1 - x^2)^(1/2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `cos`, `asin`, `atan`
